  "description": "This pickle lemonade recipe is tangy, salty, and refreshing—made with fresh dill pickle brine and aromatic lemon slices.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Dill pickles, thinly sliced lengthwise for serving (optional); Lemon slices for serving (optional); Soda water for serving (optional)\n\nNotes: This recipe reflects my preferred balance of pickle brine, lemonade, and water for a sweet-tart drink. You can adjust the proportions with additional water, lemon juice, or pickle brine to suit your own taste, keeping in mind that the lemonade will dilute further when served over ice.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The lemonade can be refrigerated in an airtight container for a week, though I'd remove the lemon rounds after a day, as they can make the drink bitter.",
